Mortar (TrimUI Brick) changes to digdat0/ACGC-Switch-Port, all behind
TARGET_MORTAR (pkgs/acgc/CMakeLists.txt defines it with TARGET_ANDROID):

- libultra.h: glibc declares bcmp/bcopy/bzero (mortar_decls.h includes them).
- pc_main.c: load GLES through SDL_GL_GetProcAddress (compat/glad/gl.h);
  a window smaller than the panel (settings.ini, default 640x480) is an
  exclusive fullscreen mode, so the compositor scales it (fill rate).
- pc_gx.c: the Switch build's vertex ring (one 8 MiB buffer, base-vertex
  draws), persistently mapped with EXT_buffer_storage: glBufferData per
  draw made the PowerVR driver allocate and map device memory each time.
- pc_gx_tev.c: the Switch build's program binary cache (the PowerVR
  compiler needs ~70 s for the 172 boot variants; ~0.1 s from the cache).
- pc_keybindings.c, pc_pad.c, pc_pause_menu.c: Brick buttons by label; the
  D-pad drives the main stick, L2 + D-pad is the GameCube D-pad.
- pc_vi.c: ACGC_FPS=1 logs the frame rate.

